---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
const updated = 'September 26, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Post and Board Media"
  description="Terms for using the Post and Board Media website and booking storefront sign placements and shared mailer spots."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Terms' }]}
>
  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container--narrow prose">
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>

      <p>These terms apply to your use of this website, operated by {site.name}. By using the site, you agree to them.</p>

      <h2>Bookings and quotes</h2>
      <p>
        Opportunities listed on this website show current availability, which we update regularly. Sending an enquiry
        lets us confirm your spot and send a quote. Your booking is confirmed when you accept the quote and pay as set
        out in it. Each quote states the placement or mailing, term or date, ad size, what’s included, the total price
        and any conditions, including cancellation terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices</h2>
      <p>Prices are in Canadian dollars. Applicable taxes are added as shown on your quote.</p>

      <h2>Your advertising content</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for the content you supply and confirm you have the right to use it. We may decline
        artwork or advertising that is misleading, unlawful or inappropriate for a public sign or mailer. Your ad is
        produced after you approve the final layout.
      </p>

      <h2>Results</h2>
      <p>
        We place your advertising as described in your quote. Like all advertising, results depend on many factors, so
        we can’t guarantee a particular number of customers, leads or sales.
      </p>

      <h2>Example layouts</h2>
      <p>Images marked “Example layout” or “Illustrative image” show how placements look. Businesses named in them are fictional.</p>

      <h2>Website content</h2>
      <p>The text, design and brand elements of this website belong to {site.name} and may not be reused without permission.</p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply there.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? {site.contact.email ? <>Email us at <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.</> : <>Reach us through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</>}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
